<?php

namespace App\Libraries;

/**
 * Eighth batch: what the assistant can MAKE now (charts, pictures of charts, PDF / Excel / CSV files), live numbers, follow-ups, and the
 * everyday problems the logs showed it missed (a "server response error", a bare "why", a bare "not helpful", typos). Answers describe
 * behaviour only; no number, limit of a standard or secret is written here. Loaded by `php spark brain:seed`.
 */
class BrainSeed8
{
    /** @return list<array<string,mixed>> */
    public static function all(): array
    {
        $o = static fn (string $label, string $url): array => ['type' => 'open', 'label' => $label, 'url' => $url];
        $k = static fn (string $title, string $keywords, string $body, array $steps = [], array $extra = []): array => array_merge(['title' => $title, 'keywords' => $keywords, 'body' => $body, 'steps' => $steps], $extra);
        $tr = ['actions' => [$o('Open Lab Tracker', 'dtr?tab=tracker')]];

        return [
            // ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ what can you do
            $k('What can you do?', 'what can you do, what do you do, your abilities, features, capabilities, how can you help, what can i ask, what are you able to do, help menu, what is possible', 'I can: (1) answer how-to questions about NEXUS-L, (2) give live numbers from the QC data (how many reports passed or failed), (3) draw charts and graphs of that data, (4) make files for you: a PDF or Excel of a report or of a list of reports, and a picture (PNG) or PDF of any chart, (5) open a report by its Lab Reference, (6) explain errors and what to check, and (7) connect you to an administrator. Just write what you want in your own words.', ['Try: "pie chart of pass and fail"', 'Try: "export failed bonding reports this month to Excel"', 'Try: "export DTP20261012FAA8-L as PDF"', 'Try: "how many reports failed this month?"']),
            $k('Can you make charts and graphs?', 'make chart, create graph, draw chart, generate graph, plot data, can you chart, visualize data, graph of reports, show chart, make a diagram, create a diagram, visualise', 'Yes. Ask for a chart in plain words and I draw it from the live QC data, for example "pie chart of pass and fail", "bar chart of failed reports by category", "trend of reports per month" or "pass vs fail by category". The chart appears in the chat; use the buttons under it to enlarge it or save it as an image (PNG) or PDF.'),
            $k('Which kinds of charts can you draw?', 'chart types, kinds of graphs, pie chart, bar chart, line chart, donut, stacked bar, trend chart, which charts, graph types available', 'Pie / donut (shares), bar (compare groups, stacked when pass / tolerable / fail are shown together) and line (a trend over days or months). Say "pie", "bar" or "line" - or just describe what you want to see and I pick the best one.'),
            $k('What can I chart by?', 'chart by, group by, break down, per category, by supplier, by month, by model, by technician, by material, dimensions of chart, what can be charted, split by', 'Reports can be grouped by category (Bonding, Fabric, Leather...), result (Pass / Tolerable / Fail), month, day, supplier, model / style, material type, technician and status. Examples: "reports by supplier", "failed reports by category", "bonding results per month". You can add a period: this month, last month, this year, last 3 months or a month name.'),
            $k('How do I make a pie chart of pass and fail?', 'pie chart pass fail, pass and fail chart, pass vs fail pie, pass fail percentage chart, results pie chart, quality pie, percentage of passed', 'Write "pie chart of pass and fail" (add a category or period if you like, for example "pie chart of fabric results this year"). The pie shows how many reports passed, were tolerable or failed, with the total in the middle.'),
            $k('How do I chart pass vs fail by category?', 'pass vs fail by category, compare categories pass fail, stacked bar categories, results by category chart, which category fails most, category quality chart', 'Write "pass vs fail by category chart". You get one bar per category, split into Pass, Tolerable and Fail, so you can see which category fails most. Add "this month" or "this year" to limit the period.'),
            $k('How do I see a trend per month?', 'trend per month, monthly trend, reports over time, line chart per month, monthly chart, how many reports each month, month by month, growth chart, history chart', 'Write "trend of reports per month" for the last 12 months. For one result or category add it: "trend of failed bonding reports per month". For days inside a month write "chart of failed bonding reports this month".'),
            $k('Chart of failed reports', 'chart of failed reports, graph of failures, failed reports chart, failure chart, defects chart, fail trend, where do we fail, failures by category, show failures', 'Write "bar chart of failed reports by category" to see where failures happen, or "trend of failed reports per month" to see if they go up or down. Add a category to narrow it: "failed bonding reports per month".'),
            $k('Can I change the chart after it is drawn?', 'change chart, modify chart, switch chart type, chart as pie, same for leather, different period, follow up chart, update chart, edit the graph, now show it as', 'Yes, just say what to change: "as a pie", "as a line", "same for leather", "this month", "only failed". I keep the last chart in mind for 30 minutes and redraw it with the change.'),
            $k('How do I save a chart as an image?', 'save chart image, download chart png, chart as picture, chart to image, create image of chart, export chart image, picture of the graph, save graph as image, png of chart, jpg chart', 'Under every chart there is an "Image (PNG)" button: it saves the chart exactly as drawn (with its title and legend) to your Downloads folder. "Enlarge" opens a bigger version, which you can save too.'),
            $k('Can you create an image or a picture?', 'create image, generate image, make a picture, draw a picture, create picture, make an image, ai image, generate photo, picture please, create an illustration, can you draw', 'I make pictures of your QC data: any chart can be saved as a PNG image. I cannot create free-hand artwork or photos, because everything I produce comes from NEXUS-L data. To put a chart in a presentation or e-mail, save it as an image with the "Image (PNG)" button.'),
            $k('How do I save a chart as a PDF?', 'chart as pdf, chart to pdf, graph pdf, download chart pdf, print chart, export chart pdf, make pdf of chart, pdf of graph', 'Press the "PDF" button under the chart. A one-page PDF with the chart is made on the server and downloads. If it says the PDF could not be made, the server needs Chrome or Edge installed; the PNG image always works.'),
            $k('How do I get the numbers behind a chart?', 'chart data excel, data of chart, numbers of the graph, export chart data, chart to excel, graph data csv, table behind chart, underlying data, chart values', 'Every chart comes with a "Data (Excel)" download of its numbers. Or say "export that to Excel" (or CSV) right after the chart.'),
            $k('Chart says no data', 'chart no data, nothing to draw, empty chart, no reports for selection, chart is empty, graph blank, no data for the chart', 'No report matches that selection, so there is nothing to draw. Try a longer period (this year, last 3 months), remove the category or result filter, or ask for "chart of reports by category" to see everything.'),
            // ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ files and export
            $k('How do I export a report as PDF?', 'export report pdf, download report pdf, report as pdf, make pdf of report, pdf of this report, give me a pdf, generate report pdf, save report pdf, download pdf of report, export this report', 'Write "export DTP20261012FAA8-L as PDF" (or "export this report as PDF" after you asked about it). I make a PDF summary of the saved report (details and every test with reading and result) and give you a download link. For the signed official sheet use the buttons that come with it: "Official report PDF" or "Open the official sheet".', [], $tr),
            $k('What is the difference between the summary PDF and the official report?', 'summary pdf vs official, official report sheet, which pdf to send, signed report vs summary, assistant pdf official, report pdf difference, what do i send to interlink', 'The summary PDF I make is a plain printout of the saved data for your records. The official report is the VF sheet (or the Access report for materials) that is approved and signed; that is the document you send to InterLink. Open it with the "Open the official sheet" button.'),
            $k('How do I export reports to Excel?', 'export excel, reports to excel, download excel, spreadsheet of reports, export to xlsx, excel file of reports, list of reports excel, export failed reports excel, make excel, give me a spreadsheet', 'Write what you want in the sentence, for example "export failed bonding reports this month to Excel" or "export all fabric reports to Excel". I make an .xlsx file with Lab Ref, application, category, material, supplier, model, dates, technician, status and result, and give you a download link.'),
            $k('Can I export to CSV?', 'export csv, csv file, comma separated, download csv, reports csv, csv format, export as csv, data as csv', 'Yes: say "csv" instead of "Excel", for example "export passed leather reports last month as CSV". The file opens in Excel with the right characters.'),
            $k('Can I export a list of reports as PDF?', 'list of reports pdf, export list pdf, pdf of failed reports, printable list, report list pdf, pdf table of reports, print the list', 'Yes: "give me a PDF of failed fabric reports this month". The PDF is a landscape table of the matching reports. Excel is better for more than about 1,500 rows.'),
            $k('Can I export one test of a report?', 'export report to excel, tests of a report excel, report readings excel, results of one report, export readings, one report excel, export report csv', 'Write "export DTP20261012FAA8-L to Excel": the file lists every test of that report with method, requirement, reading and result.'),
            $k('How long does the download link work?', 'download link expires, link expired, file no longer available, how long file, download link valid, file gone, expired download', 'A link works for one hour and only for the person who asked for the file. After that ask me again and I make a fresh one - it takes a few seconds.'),
            $k('Where is my downloaded file?', 'where is my file, find downloaded file, file downloaded where, downloads folder, cannot find the file, where did pdf go', 'The browser saves it to your Downloads folder (or asks where, depending on your browser settings). The chat shows the file name on the button; look for that name.'),
            $k('The file did not download', 'download failed, file not downloading, button does nothing, cannot download file, download blocked, no file, export not working, link not working', 'Check that the browser did not block the download (look for a blocked-download icon in the address bar), then press the button again. If it says the file is no longer available, ask me again: links expire after an hour.'),
            $k('The PDF could not be made', 'pdf could not be made, pdf failed, cannot create pdf, pdf error, pdf not generated, no pdf, chrome required pdf, pdf engine', 'PDFs are printed by Chrome or Edge on the server. If that is missing or busy I tell you so. Excel and CSV exports do not need it, and charts can always be saved as PNG. Tell an administrator if PDFs never work.', [], ['diagnose' => 'pdf_engine']),
            $k('How many files can I make?', 'file limit, export limit, how many exports, too many files, limit exports per hour, rate limit export, max rows export', 'Up to 20 files per hour per person, and up to 5,000 rows in one export. A bigger list is cut at 5,000 rows - narrow it with a category, result or period.'),
            $k('Who can see the files I make?', 'file security, who can open my export, private download, are files private, share file link, other users download', 'Only you: the link is tied to your login and stops working after an hour. Files are removed from the server after a day. To share, download the file and send it yourself.'),
            $k('Export that to Excel', 'export that, export it, download that, save that to excel, export these results, export the result, download this data, send me that as excel, that to csv', 'Right after I show a chart or numbers, say "export that to Excel" (or CSV) and I make a file of what you just saw. If I have nothing to refer to, I ask which reports you mean.'),
            // ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ live numbers
            $k('How many reports failed?', 'how many failed, number of failures, failed count, total fail, how many reports failed, failure count, count of failed reports, how many fail this month', 'Ask it as a question: "how many reports failed this month?" or "how many bonding tests failed?". I count them live from the QC data and show passed, failed and tolerable. Add "chart" to see it as a picture.'),
            $k('How do I find reports by supplier or model?', 'search reports supplier, find reports by model, list reports for supplier, search by style, find report by material, lookup reports, find failed reports of supplier', 'Write "find reports for <supplier or model>" (for example "find bonding reports for VERO"). I list the matches with an Open button each; for a spreadsheet say "export them to Excel".'),
            $k('Can you tell me the pass rate?', 'pass rate, percentage passed, quality rate, overall pass percentage, what percent pass, success rate of tests, how good is quality, defect rate', 'Ask "what is the pass rate for bonding this month?" - I show passed, failed and tolerable with percentages from the live data. A "pie chart of pass and fail" shows the same as a picture.'),
            // ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ everyday problems
            $k('I get a server response error', 'server response error, server error, response error, server responce error, error from server, 500 error, internal server error, request failed, something went wrong, server not responding', 'A server error means a request to NEXUS-L failed on the server. Try once more (Ctrl + F5 to reload). If it repeats: note the page and what you pressed, check whether other pages work, and tell an administrator - the time of the error helps them find it in the logs. If the page works but one button fails, the message under the button usually says what to fix.', ['Reload with Ctrl + F5 and try again.', 'Check that another page opens (to tell a single feature from a server problem).', 'Write down the page, the button and the time.', 'Tell an administrator if it happens again.']),
            $k('The page is slow or not loading', 'page slow, not loading, loading forever, website slow, takes long to open, stuck loading, laggy, slow connection, spinning, freezes, hangs', 'On a slow connection you see grey placeholder blocks and a progress bar at the top; the page is still loading. Wait a few seconds, or reload with Ctrl + F5. If it stays stuck, check your network (other sites open?) and tell an administrator if only NEXUS-L is slow.'),
            $k('Why?', 'why, why not, how come, why is that, why did that happen, reason, what is the reason, explain why, why is it so', 'Tell me what you mean by "why" - which message, error or number are you asking about? Write the question in a sentence, for example "why did the report fail?" or "why is the PDF date different?", and I explain.'),
            $k('That did not help', 'not helpful, did not help, that is wrong, not what i asked, useless answer, wrong answer, you did not understand, incorrect, not correct, bad answer', 'Sorry about that. Please say it in other words, or tell me the page and what you are trying to do. I have noted the question so it can be improved, and I can connect you to an administrator if you prefer.'),
            $k('I do not know what to ask', 'dont know what to ask, what should i ask, i need help, help me, i am lost, where do i start, give me an example, example questions, what can i say, suggestions', 'Here are some things to try: "how do I send a report to InterLink?", "how many reports failed this month?", "pie chart of pass and fail", "export failed bonding reports to Excel", "open DTP20261012FAA8-L", or "I get an error when I press Send". Or describe your problem in your own words.'),
            $k('Do you understand typing mistakes?', 'typo, spelling mistake, misspelled, wrong spelling, do you understand typos, spelling errors, bad grammar, abbreviations', 'Yes, small spelling mistakes are fine ("reprot", "responce error", "grap of failed"). If I am still not sure, I show related topics so you can pick one.'),
            $k('Can I give you a command in my own words?', 'natural language, plain words, own words, talk normally, how to phrase, do i need exact words, speak naturally, command format', 'Yes, write it the way you would tell a colleague: "give me a pdf of that report", "show failed bonding this month as a graph", "send me the failed list in Excel". You do not need special words.'),
            $k('Does the assistant remember what we talked about?', 'remember conversation, context memory, follow up question, previous question, remember earlier, same as before, continue conversation, and then, what about', 'Within a conversation, yes: short follow-ups such as "and for leather?", "as a pie", "export that" or "why?" refer to what we just discussed. Charts are remembered for 30 minutes.'),
            $k('Is the data in the chart live?', 'live data chart, real time data, up to date numbers, is chart current, data fresh, how current is the data, refreshed, latest data', 'Yes, every chart and count is read from the QC database at the moment you ask. Ask again later to refresh it.'),
            $k('Why do the numbers differ from the Lab Tracker?', 'numbers differ, different count, chart does not match tracker, wrong total, counts do not match, mismatch numbers, other number in tracker', 'I count reports by the date they were tested and by their saved result (Pass, Tolerable, Fail; anything else is "Other"). The tracker may filter by other dates or statuses. Tell me the exact filter and I can match it, or ask an administrator to compare.'),
            $k('Which results are counted as Other?', 'other results, unrated, what is other, unknown result, results not pass fail, p w/u, pwu, other in chart, unrated reports', 'Reports with no clear Pass, Tolerable or Fail (for example unrated or special codes) are grouped as "Other" in charts. The report itself shows its own rating.'),
            $k('Can the assistant change or delete reports?', 'assistant edit report, bot delete report, modify data, can you change report, change results, update report, assistant write data, delete data', 'No. I only read data and make files and charts. Reports are changed in QC Lab Reports by people with access, and every change is recorded.'),
            $k('Who can use charts and exports?', 'who can export, permissions chart, access to exports, user rights export, restricted export, role export, can everyone export', 'Every signed-in user can ask for charts and exports of the QC data they can see in NEXUS-L. The files contain report details but no passwords or personal data, and links work only for the requester.'),
        ];
    }
}
